只输出严格JSON，恰好包含id（metadata.id原样）、summary_zh（15到140个Unicode字符，通常40到100字）、category（枚举）、tags（2到5个不重复关键词，每个最多30字符）、confidence（0到1，仅自评）、insufficient_evidence（布尔）、evidence（1到3个对象，每个恰好包含paragraph_id、fact）、limitations（0到5个字符串）。只选择输入中长度20至120字符的完整片段编号；fact是该片段支持的中文事实转述。不要输出quote，不要自行抄写、拼接、删改或补造引用。程序会按编号附上原文。一个编号只用一次；最多3条证据。不得增加字段。
摘要和limitations保留会改变功能意义的前提、平台例外和限制：设密码后才认证、页面保持打开才提醒、依赖外部组件、估算不等于保证。只写已实现功能，不将规划当完成。证据不足就标记，不编造。
图像识别/分类不是媒体创作，没有贴切类别归other；量化、计算与领域研究归search-research，不因多智能体实现归agents-automation；模型/CLI适配与插件开发工具归coding-development；市场/精选目录按搜索发现归search-research。不要按附属同步、备份或评论功能分类。不要推断本机客户端等于本地模型。
摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Recall (撤回), edit-and-resend (编辑重发) and regenerate (重新生成) for DeepSeek Harness conversation messages — Web and Desktop plugin","id":"gh:1339400021","install_available":true,"language":"JavaScript","name":"dsh-retrace","slug":"yamingmou/dsh-retrace","topics":["chat","deepseek","deepseek-harness","dsh","dsh-plugin","dsh-plugins","edit","message-editor","plugin","recall"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Recall (撤回), edit-and-resend (编辑重发) and regenerate (重新生成) for DeepSeek Harness conversation messages"},{"id":"p1s2","text":" — Web and Desktop plugin"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# 🧭 dsh-retrace"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"**Recall · Resend (restart from here) · Regenerate**, plus **write-safe** in-conversation\nversioning"},{"id":"p3s2","text":" — the **Agent business layer (production-grade guarantees)** for\nDeepSeek Harness."},{"id":"p4s1","text":"**English** · 简体中文"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"**Recall / resend / regenerate** — the three moves every conversation\ndeserves. But rewinding is not"},{"id":"p5s2","text":" just \"delete a message\": DeepSeek Harness stores\nconversations in an append-only event log, so a re"},{"id":"p5s3","text":"call only rewinds the context\nwhile changed **artifact files stay changed**. dsh-retrace versions th"},{"id":"p5s4","text":"e\nconversation **and its artifacts** together, and keeps **every new rewind legal** —\nit cannot dirt"},{"id":"p5s5","text":"y the log, and new markers create **no token-meter pairing debt**\n(two-segment atomic pairs land by "},{"id":"p5s6","text":" new markers create **no token-meter pairing debt**\n(two-segment atomic pairs land by construction)."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"> ⚠️ **Honest scope (matches the companion contract's own note)**: sessions that\n> already contain *"},{"id":"p6s2","text":"*legacy single-segment markers** — written by older versions —\n> are **known design debt**. Before `"},{"id":"p6s3","text":"/compact`, run the companion `check` and\n> clean them up (`fix --remove-markers`); otherwise the hos"},{"id":"p6s4","text":"t's own pre-compaction\n> self-check blocks compaction. New rewinds do not add to that debt."},{"id":"p7s1","text":"> 🛡️ **Write safety** · 🔍 **Deep offline checks** · 🔄 **Detect → repair → guard** — see below."},{"id":"p8s1","text":"> Versions: VERSIONS.md"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"> **0.4.148 is the current release** — install/pin `0.4.148` (the **GitHub Release is out; the npm p"},{"id":"p9s2","text":"ackage is still pending** — the latest npm version is `0.4.139`; see VERSIONS.md). The `dsh-retrace@"},{"id":"p9s3","text":"0.4.148` examples below apply to this release."},{"id":"p10s1","text":"## ✨ Features"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"| Action | Where | What happens |"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"### 5. Requirements"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"- DeepSeek Harness providing the peer packages listed in `package.json`\n(`@deepseek-ai/dsh-session`,"},{"id":"p14s2","text":" `@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-*`, `cordis`, `react` — the\ncurrent build targets the `0.1.7-rc.2` generat"},{"id":"p14s3","text":"ion).\n- `dsh-log-contract >= 0.3.18` (installed automatically as a dependency).\n- The plugin declare"},{"id":"p14s4","text":"s the host capabilities it needs via `inject`\n(`sessions`, `agents`, `webServer`, `fs`, `subprocess`"},{"id":"p14s5","text":", `sandboxPolicy`, `jobs`).\nA missing capability degrades the corresponding feature (for example, no"},{"id":"p14s6","text":"\n`subprocess` ⇒ rollback uses the built-in snapshots only); it does not block boot."},{"id":"p15s1","text":"## 🧠 How it works"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"1. **Host core** (`lib/host-core.js`, zero runtime imports) locates the target\nmessage in the sessio"},{"id":"p17s2","text":"n's live surface, computes the shadow span\n`[message … last surface node]`, and appends one replacem"},{"id":"p17s3","text":"ent\n`assistant/message` with an **empty** body — a valid surface node that\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"## 🔺 Compatibility & upgrade notes"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"`dsh-retrace` is a **bundle plugin**: it plugs into whatever host surface it is\ninstalled into. A ho"},{"id":"p19s2","text":"st release that *removes* a package or a client service can\ntherefore break an older plugin build ev"},{"id":"p19s3","text":"en though nothing in that build changed —\nthe symptom is usually a failed boot, not a wrong-looking "},{"id":"p19s4","text":"h nothing in that build changed —\nthe symptom is usually a failed boot, not a wrong-looking feature."},{"id":"p20s1","text":"This section exists so you can tell **host-side breakage** from **plugin-side bugs**.\nRead it before"},{"id":"p20s2","text":"ts so you can tell **host-side breakage** from **plugin-side bugs**.\nRead it before filing an issue."},{"id":"p21s1","text":"### Compatibility & runtime contract (for marketplace review)"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"| Item | Declaration |"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"| **Node.js** | `>=20.0.0` (see `package.json#engines`) |\n| **DSH** | `>=0.1.5 <0.3.0` (see `package"},{"id":"p23s2","text":".json#dsh.compatibility`); desktop and web modes supported |\n| **Runtime files** | All files needed "},{"id":"p23s3","text":"at runtime are **committed** in this repository and declared in `package.json#files` (`lib/**`, `cor"},{"id":"p23s4","text":"dis.patch.yml`, `README*.md`, `HUMANS.txt`, `LICENSE`) |\n| **Build output** | Build output is commit"},{"id":"p23s5","text":"ted (`lib/client.bundle.js`, `lib/dynamic-client.js`, `lib/dynamic-host.js`) and reproducible in-rep"},{"id":"p23s6","text":"o: `pnpm i && pnpm build` (`scripts/generate-dynamic.mjs`, `scripts/build-client.mjs`) |\n| **Runtime"},{"id":"p23s7","text":" dependencies** | `dsh-log-contract` (log-contract validation), `zod` (argument validation). No post"},{"id":"p23s8","text":"-install scripts, no network access, no additional code download |\n| **Peer dependencies** | `@deeps"},{"id":"p23s9","text":"eek-ai/cordis` and DSH client packages (provided by DSH itself, not bundled or redistributed here) |"},{"id":"p23s10","text":"\n| **Permissions / external services** | Reads and writes only the local DSH session data directory "},{"id":"p23s11","text":"and session logs. No external services, no telemetry, no data upload |\n| **Failure bounds** | Every "},{"id":"p23s12","text":"write (recall / edit / restore / rollback) backs up outside the target file first, then performs fra"},{"id":"p23s13","text":"me-level verification and resurfacing checks. On any failure it aborts and leaves the original untou"},{"id":"p23s14","text":"ched; ambiguous cases are refused with an actionable message instead of degrading silently |\n| **Rev"},{"id":"p23s15","text":"ersibility** | Each operation has a documented reversible path; local management scripts can roll ba"},{"id":"p23s16","text":"ck to the previous snapshot |"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"## ⚠️ Requirements & limitations"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"- Only **user messages** can be re-sent from; recall works on user and assistant\nmessages. Tool resu"},{"id":"p25s2","text":"lts are shadowed along with the recalled range but are not\nthemselves recall targets.\n- A recall tha"},{"id":"p25s3","text":"t targets a running turn **pauses it first** (official stop entry, bounded\nwait). If the pause fails"},{"id":"p25s4","text":" or times out, the recall continues and a notice tells you so.\nTrue restore and rollback preview req"},{"id":"p25s5","text":"uire an **idle** session; they are rejected\notherwise.\n- Recall/resend operate on the **active model"},{"id":"p25s6","text":" surface**: a message that was\nalready compacted away or previously recalled is rejected\n(`target-sh"},{"id":"p25s7","text":"adowed`), and a message whose write has not flushed yet is reported as\n`message-pending` (\"still bei"},{"id":"p25s8","text":"ng generated\") rather than being misreported as gone.\n- Regenerate re-sends only the **text** of the"},{"id":"p25s9","text":" original prompt; prompts that\ncarried images fall back to the text-only content.\n- File **restore**"},{"id":"p25s10","text":" is text-only: a non-UTF-8 (binary) file is reported as\n`binary-unsupported` and skipped instead of "},{"id":"p25s11","text":"being written back. **Export as…**\npackages the captured preimage bytes (including non-text files) w"},{"id":"p25s12","text":"ithout restoring\nanything.\n- True restore edits the session log **in place** (it neutralizes the two"},{"id":"p25s13","text":" marker\nsegments; sequence numbers stay as they are). It refuses to run while the session is\nthe one"},{"id":"p25s14","text":" you are viewing, while it is running, or while another process holds the file,\nand you must reopen "},{"id":"p25s15","text":"the session (or refresh) to see the result."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
